## Lore

The line soldiers of the Transgalactic Empire. Any race can serve in the
Legions, though the kreeghor dominate them. Training covers space and ground
combat and is harsh enough that the book measures it against the U.S. Marines
and calls their boot camp a Boy Scout trip by comparison.

Obedience is emphasized over initiative. Following orders at any cost is held to
be the most important thing a soldier can do, and most kreeghor do it very well.
Some members of other races have been less willing to obey blindly - and one
such refusal is what started the revolution that still plagues the Empire.

## Deserters

The Free World Council is full of them. Other Legionnaire deserters have gone to
be spacers, pirates, runners, mercenaries and adventurers. All of them are
traitors by Imperial law and all of them are subject to the death penalty if the
Empire takes them alive.

## GM Notes

Available as a player character with the Game Master''s approval.

Two things on the sheet will look wrong and are not. The class is granted Hand
to Hand: Basic AND Hand to Hand: Expert, because the book trains it separately
for zero gravity and for normal gravity and the catalog has one family for both.
And Imperial Battle Armor reads 90 M.D.C. where a kreeghor Legionnaire should
have 100 - the gear row holds one number and the book prints two.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'imperial-legionnaire');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'imperial-legionnaire';

